{
    "file": "Customer_Support_Management.docx",
    "title": "Customer Support Management",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Effective customer support management requires more than resolving individual requests. It requires a structured operating approach that connects customer needs, support channels, people, processes, service standards, technology, escalation, knowledge, performance measurement, and continuous improvement. When these elements work together, support teams can provide reliable service while controlling workload, improving resolution quality, and strengthening the overall customer experience.",
        "This course equips managers, supervisors, and team leaders with practical methods for organizing and managing customer support operations. Participants will learn how to define service standards, structure support workflows, manage queues and priorities, improve first-contact resolution, establish escalation processes, build useful knowledge resources, coach support employees, handle difficult cases, monitor service performance, and use customer-support data to improve processes and decisions.",
        "The program combines operational management with customer-experience principles. Participants will work through support scenarios, workflow analysis, service-level exercises, escalation cases, performance measures, coaching situations, and improvement planning to develop a practical approach for leading responsive, consistent, and customer-focused support teams."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Customer-support managers, customer-service managers, supervisors, team leaders, contact-center leaders, help-desk managers, service-desk personnel, branch and operations managers, customer-experience professionals, service-quality personnel, and employees responsible for managing customer requests, support teams, service levels, escalations, or support performance."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "The course uses an interactive methodology combining short presentations, customer-support case studies, workflow mapping, service-level exercises, queue and prioritization scenarios, escalation simulations, complaint and difficult-customer cases, performance-measurement activities, coaching exercises, root-cause analysis, group discussions, and action planning. Participants will apply the tools to realistic support environments and develop practical improvements relevant to their own operations."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Customer support operations management",
        "Service standards management",
        "Workflow and queue management",
        "Prioritization and escalation",
        "Customer communication",
        "Case and complaint management",
        "Knowledge management",
        "Support-team leadership",
        "Performance coaching",
        "Service performance measurement",
        "Root-cause analysis",
        "Continuous support improvement"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Explain the role of customer support within the overall customer experience.",
        "Design clear support workflows from initial contact through resolution and closure.",
        "Establish practical service standards and service-level expectations.",
        "Prioritize customer cases according to urgency, impact, complexity, and agreed criteria.",
        "Develop effective escalation paths and ownership rules.",
        "Improve first-contact resolution while maintaining quality and accuracy.",
        "Manage customer communication throughout the support process.",
        "Use knowledge resources to improve consistency and reduce avoidable repeat work.",
        "Coach and manage support employees using relevant operational and quality measures.",
        "Analyze support data, recurring contacts, and complaints to identify root causes.",
        "Develop practical actions for improving support efficiency, quality, and customer satisfaction."
    ],
